Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:19:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/18] nemotron: the checkpoint's NVFP4 experts at
 decode-sized calls take 32 columns a warp and four steps of loads in flight,
 same bits

ck_experts.cu's grouped kernel is a template over a warp's n8 tiles and the steps of codes, scales and weights it
keeps in registers ahead of the mma. Prompt chunks keep 8 tiles and one step; calls of up to launch.few_rows token
rows take the _few pair, 4 tiles and 4 steps (125-128 registers, no spills). Each column still takes its 64-input
steps in order through the same mma_fp4 and the epilogue is unchanged. Ck.down takes the call's token rows to choose.
The modelopt test checks up and down at 1 and 16 token rows byte-equal to the same pairs inside a 40-row call.
